<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-1683</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> The entrance to SCP-1683 is to be sealed and the interior monitored by security personnel. No personnel above D-Class are permitted into SCP-1683's interior. A containment site has been set up in the residence connected to SCP-1683, with several other homes in the neighborhood having been purchased in order to create a buffer between civilian residences and SCP-1683. A cover story regarding ongoing construction work has been implemented, pending further developments in SCP-1683's containment method.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-1683 is a children's bedroom, located on the second floor of a two-story residential home. SCP-1683 contains one furnished bed, a dresser, one telescope, a ceiling covered in luminescent space-themed stickers, and several pieces of media regarding space travel. Notably, the residence's second floor contains no windows.</p>
<p>Subjects entering SCP-1683 will note the realism and detail put into the stickers, which are all located on the ceiling of SCP-1683. Analysis has shown that they accurately map many known star systems and planetary locations. As the subject continues to observe the stickers, they will begin to accurately mimic the current appearance of the night sky, although satellites and other airborne objects will not be visible.</p>
<p>When a subject interacts with the telescope located within SCP-1683, they will claim to see the constellations, and be able to name them despite any previous knowledge. Once all currently visible constellations have been identified, the entrance to the room will become sealed from the inside, and impossible to open. Attempting to enter SCP-1683 via alternate means has not been attempted due to the possibly irreversible damage to SCP-1683.</p>
<p>After twenty minutes, it will become possible to enter SCP-1683. There will be no sign of any subjects previously occupying it. At the same time, orbiting satellites will report a sudden human-shaped anomaly in space appearing approximately 2000 kilometers over the surface of the earth, heading into deep space. Analysis has shown that the subjects appear to be identical to those who entered SCP-1683.</p>
<p>SCP-1683 was discovered in 1971, following a set of police reports detailing SCP-1683's effect. The subject originally residing within SCP-1683, a young adult male, had gone missing directly prior to the first recorded manifestation of SCP-1683's effect. The subjects parents described him as having a deep interest in space exploration, which they had discouraged due to his isolation from peers. Neighbors reported rarely seeing the subject outside of his home, and some were unaware of his existence. It is currently believed that the subject initiated SCP-1683's effect, although how he did so is unknown.</p>
<p>As of 8/19/1976, SCP-1683 has been classified as Safe.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum:</strong> Documentation recovered from classified U.S and Russian Federation records indicate that on 12/25/1969, satellites indicated that a small humanoid, appearing to be wearing some form of spacesuit, suddenly manifested and began rapidly moving away from the earth's surface. This was followed by several other unknown objects, believed to be supplies.</p>
